have SysAdmins with the generosity to set up such groups.

Another issue: on systems with draconian file-reading policies, how can
legitimate file sharing take place without the possibility of punishment?
I think that the writers of these policies should at least include 
clauses that legitimacize public file sharing via ~/pub directories or
some similar mechanism.

