Another solution is to create some directory in your home directory
mode 711 called (by way of example) dist.  Now, create directories
mode 755 (or whatever you want) under dist with obscure names, like
maybe dist/tomary.7452.  Although these directories are available to
anyone, you have to know the name of the directory to get into it, and
you cannot ls dist since it is not readable (but can cd through it
since it is executable).  Presumably, the above would be to a person
named mary, and the number on the end would have been agreed on
beforehand.  find and other similar programs also won't be able to go
through the dist directory, since they depend on being able to get a
list of paths to recurse.

