and 'crack'ed it from there.

>I hope Mr. Henderson gets a good lawyer...

Yeah. He'll need it. UHouston has been rather rude about things like
this in the past. I was there for a year myself, and left before
anything this severe happened. I do not remember any policy like they've
got now though. In my situation it was even stupider. In one of my
classes where the instructor gave use the outline for the program,
myself an another student were accused of copying each others program.
The reason for this was that the style of the program was the same,
eventhough the actual code that did the work was different. They tried
to tell us that we just changed what the code did in order to make it
look different. What happened is there is an editor on VMS called LSE,
language sensitive editor, it does things such as if you put a begin and
hit a keystroke, it fills in the end and a blank core. This lets you
just put the code in. Well it does this with everything including
comments. So if two users use this they will have the same spacing and
look to the program. They didn't care if the code was different in the
CS dept., it just mattered that they *looked* alike. Luckily if you take
it far enough, there was a board that reviews it and ridicules the
professor for you. I mean they correct the wrong.

Just thought I'd add my experience with UHou.

