IRC is a tool which can be used for business use (e.g. remote conferences),
academic use (e.g. discussion of academic subjects or projects), recreational 
or any number of other uses (file transfer, combinations of other uses, etc.) 
Your question is like the question "Is the telephone considered recreational 
or trivial use?"

To subject a student to disciplinary measures for using IRC, in absence of 
prior warnings or policy statements *specifically mentioning IRC* is a case
of of arbitrary punishment without due process or attempt at fairness.
It would reflect very poorly upon an institution.

